  "id": "moderating-effect",
  "term": "moderating effect",
  "definition": "A moderating effect is when a third factor changes how strongly two other variables are related. In this study, psychological resilience acted as a moderator by weakening the link between smartphone addiction and depression symptoms, and also between bedtime procrastination and depression symptoms.",
